# What never reaches a deployment.
#
# This file replaces .gitignore for the upload, so everything that must stay
# off the build has to be named here — starting with the env files. A local
# .env.local uploaded with the source would both ship secrets into the build
# and override the variables configured on the project.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Notes with keys in them. .gitignore has the same rules; here they are
# narrowed to document extensions, because lib/supabase/secret-env.ts is a
# source file the build needs and `*secret*` would have taken it out.
*.rtf
*key*.txt
*secret*.txt
*secret*.json
credentials*

.git/
.next/
node_modules/
*.tsbuildinfo
.DS_Store

# 144 MB of PDFs: the input to the importers in .tools/, already turned into
# rows in the database. Nothing at runtime reads them.
/Олимпиады_по_*/

# Scripts that run against the database from a laptop, not from the server.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash, every one of them. Without it these patterns
# match at any depth, the way .gitignore does: a bare `supabase/` also took out
# lib/supabase/, and the build failed on a missing @/lib/supabase/admin.
/.tools/
/scripts/
/supabase/
/docs/
